Cardano Scala Lab
Original research prototype code, 2026.
Original code is Apache-2.0 except the explicitly attributed MIT adaptations
core/src/main/java/lab/vrf/Ed25519Point.java and Draft03Math.java. Their source
notices and fixtures/vrf/licenses/CCL-LICENSE are retained unchanged.

This source distribution includes fixtures from Cardano Ledger and Plutus,
and reference cost parameters from Scalus. Original upstream licenses and
notices are retained under fixtures/licenses. See docs/fixture-provenance.md,
docs/vm-conformance.md and docs/vm-provenance.json for immutable provenance.

Scalus is a runtime dependency; no Scalus implementation source or DiLF4S
implementation is vendored. Third-party dependencies retain their licenses.

Handshake/mux research also includes manually specified and source-derived
fixtures from Scalus-node and Ouroboros Network. Their Apache-2.0 licenses and
applicable NOTICE files are retained in fixtures/licenses. See
docs/network-conformance.md and docs/network-fixtures.json. No upstream
networking runtime implementation is vendored.

The bounded ledger predicate corpus contains byte-preserved Haskell ledger
integration tests distributed through cardano-blueprint and Amaru. Their
upstream licenses/notices and pinned source provenance are retained under
fixtures/licenses and fixtures/ledger. See docs/ledger-conservation.md.

Strict public-input Ed25519 research includes public-only sodium, speccheck,
Wycheproof and ledger fixture projections, archived oracle results and source
provenance. Full ISC, Apache-2.0 and MIT/CC0/BSD attribution files are retained
under fixtures/witness/licenses. The Weavechain 0.1.3 arithmetic artifact is a
runtime dependency; no signing implementation or private-key corpus is vendored.
See docs/witness-provenance.md and docs/witness-verification.md.

Required payment-key coverage adds the byte-preserved MissingVKeyWitnessesUTXOW
sequence and generator assertion from the same pinned Haskell/Blueprint/Amaru
corpus. Existing fixtures/licenses attribution applies. Original bytes,
public-only oracle observations and provenance are in fixtures/coverage;
see docs/required-key-coverage.md. No new runtime dependency is introduced.

Experimental public-only draft03 VRF verification adapts Bloxbean CCL
Ed25519Point.java and VrfUtil.java at commit
45906b783973b4c44ac6883253af26bdd07bc1b4 under MIT. The full CCL
copyright/permission notice is retained in fixtures/vrf/licenses/CCL-LICENSE.
Cardano sodium source-derived public fixtures/instrumentation retain ISC
notice in fixtures/vrf/licenses/sodium-LICENSE. Bouncy Castle's notice is
retained alongside it. No native binary, prover, signer or keygen is bundled.
See docs/vrf-verification.md for exact modifications and evidence limits.

Closed transfer fee/size research retains Apache-2.0 ledger, generator, Blueprint
and API source/fixture evidence under fixtures/fee-size, including full licenses
and generator NOTICE. Source-derived boundaries are not archived ledger failures.
See docs/fee-size-predicates.md. No native binary or runtime dependency is added.

Pure ChainSync research adds byte-preserved serialization examples and placeholder
envelope goldens from Ouroboros Consensus, Apache-2.0. Its original LICENSE and
NOTICE are retained under fixtures/chain-sync. Existing Ouroboros Network and
Scalus-node notices apply to manually specified/source-derived envelopes.
No upstream networking or consensus runtime source is vendored. See docs/chain-sync.md.

The public export omits fixtures/chain-fetch, fixtures/post-byron,
fixtures/body-commitment, fixtures/block-evidence and their corresponding
historical-index/post-byron/body-commitment/block-evidence test resources.
Provider redistribution permission for portions of that research corpus is not
established. Those bytes and the old research Git history are not distributed.
Optional private-corpus test source requires separately and lawfully obtained
data; it is not executed or counted by the public verification profile.
See docs/public-profile.md and docs/public-export-provenance.md.

Pure BlockFetch research retains pinned Ouroboros Network codec/type/serialization
and limit sources, and Ouroboros Consensus server source and Conway golden-derived
payload, under Apache-2.0. Original LICENSE and NOTICE files are retained as
fixtures/licenses/block-fetch-{network,consensus}-{LICENSE,NOTICE}. Source-derived
wire envelopes are not captured upstream runtime transcripts. Shared framing
mechanics are extracted from this project's original ChainSyncWire implementation.
See docs/block-fetch-provenance.md and fixtures/network/block-fetch/manifest.json.

Operational-certificate signature research retains the exact ledger OCert source
and four public Amaru header fixtures with their Apache-2.0 LICENSE/NOTICE files
under fixtures/opcert/evidence. The Scala adapter is original public-only code
over the existing strict Ed25519 primitive; no full crypto provider is imported.
See fixtures/opcert/README.md and docs/operational-certificates.md for source pins,
research-oracle provenance and deliberately limited acceptance claims.

